      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "Given the seven-digit number $854n526$ is divisible by 11.\n\nFor a number to be divisible by 11, the alternating sum of its digits must be divisible by 11. Start by finding the alternating sum of the digits:\n\n${8}-{5}-{4}+n-{5}-{2}+{6}=\\boxed{2+n}$\n\nSince $n$ must be a single digit (0--9), for $n+1$ to be divisible by 11, we want $n+n+1$ to be divisible by 11.\n\nNo single-digit number adds up to a multiple of 11, so there is no $n$ that will result in divisibility by $11$ for the given seven-digit number $854n526$.\nThus, $n$ in the number must be $\\boxed{0}$.",
